                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "anatopisms"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8b3554c5-c53d-3d00-b1ee-953a7d0a6e9b",
                        "entry_id": "ae71eb1d-b614-3c83-a572-a92919101c71",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A thing that is out of its proper place; the geographic counterpart to anachronism."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cbb7b954-b9e4-4541-a45f-a35b31d02cd3",
                                "sense_id": "8b3554c5-c53d-3d00-b1ee-953a7d0a6e9b",
                                "text": "A war elephant described rampaging through Tenochtitlan in a novel about the Aztec Empire would be an anatopism."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e1165ff-4226-4d6d-91cd-3093dc5b04ec",
                                "sense_id": "8b3554c5-c53d-3d00-b1ee-953a7d0a6e9b",
                                "text": "[…] and can find no associates in size at a less distance than two centuries; and in arranging which the puzzled librarian must commit an anachronism in order to avoid an anatopism."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5997096c-f053-4424-9b94-ce8aba90d791",
                                "sense_id": "8b3554c5-c53d-3d00-b1ee-953a7d0a6e9b",
                                "text": "There is no anachronism in putting them together; it is a sort of anatopism rather; the painter has placed within our view two scenes which no mortal eye could have witnessed at the same time."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "726bcf19-632d-4d66-81b0-5af171355efb",
                                "sense_id": "8b3554c5-c53d-3d00-b1ee-953a7d0a6e9b",
                                "text": "It is a remarkable fact that, so far as I can judge, no case of local inconsistency, not a single anatopism, can be brought home to the Iliad."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2154c763-7966-4a85-bee7-5f43b6baf1b7",
                                "sense_id": "8b3554c5-c53d-3d00-b1ee-953a7d0a6e9b",
                                "text": "Much of the literature on the 'Japanese Miracle' (as well as on that vast anatopism, the transfer of Japanese recipes to Western countries) expatiates on […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c45528ae-103a-49a6-9156-325b2d17bbd3",
                                "sense_id": "8b3554c5-c53d-3d00-b1ee-953a7d0a6e9b",
                                "text": "[…] the semiotic mechanism of reorganizing space in this manner as an anatopism. Anatopism renders places such as Bali equivalents of other places […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
